Subject: [PATCH 09/19] terrain: global height map + analytic height scan,
 level-1 terrain config, scan autoencoder

- supermimic/terrain/heightmap.py: rasterises the terrain geoms of the compiled model (upright boxes, height fields,
  planes) into one height map; nearest-cell lookup without horizontal gradient; 17 x 11 yaw-aligned height scan.
- supermimic/terrain/terrain_cfg.py: curriculum grid (flat, pyramid stairs up / down, uneven stairs, slope, rough),
  10 levels, risers 5-20 cm, tread 30 cm, 20 x 14 m tiles (a whole LAFAN1 clip fits without re-centring).
- supermimic/terrain/scan_ae.py: height-scan autoencoder (encoder to be frozen for the actor).
- tests/test_heightmap.py: map vs MuJoCo ray casts, lookup sign, scan order, gradient only through the height.
